  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1018 PM CDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nThe big question for the weekend is the trick-or-treat forecast. As \nwe get into Saturday, the ridge breaks down as a trough approaches \nfrom the west. PWATs will be on the rise Saturday as moisture \nstreams back into the area, and thus rain chances will increase. The \nbright side for Halloween is that rain chances are low (15-30%) for \nareas west of I-24 Saturday afternoon and evening with most of the \nrain looking to hold off until Saturday night and into Sunday. While \nthis rain is welcome, it unfortunately won't even put a dent in the \ndrought with totals through the weekend expected to be less than an \ninch.\n\nAnother storm system approaches from the west on Tuesday, bringing \nanother round of rain in the mid-week period. This looks to be our \nbest chance at meaningful rainfall. Highest rain totals should favor \nareas west of the Plateau where current probabilities give about a \n70% of at least one inch and a 30-40% of some locations picking up \ncloser to two inches before next week is over.",
